       nscd - name service cache daemon

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       nnssccdd is a daemon that provides a cache for the most common name service
       requests.   The  default configuration file, _/_e_t_c_/_n_s_c_d_._c_o_n_f, determines
       the behavior of the cache daemon.  See nnssccdd..ccoonnff(5).

       nnssccdd provides caching for accesses of the ppaasssswwdd(5), ggrroouupp(5), hhoossttss(5)
       sseerrvviicceess(5) and _n_e_t_g_r_o_u_p databases through  standard  libc  interfaces,
       such  as ggeettppwwnnaamm(3), ggeettppwwuuiidd(3), ggeettggrrnnaamm(3), ggeettggrrggiidd(3), ggeetthhoossttbbyy‐‐
       nnaammee(3), and others.

       There are two caches for each database: a positive one for items found,
       and a negative one for items not found.  Each cache has a separate  TTL
       (time‐to‐live)  period  for  its  data.   Note  that the shadow file is
       specifically not cached.  ggeettssppnnaamm(3) calls remain uncached  as  a  re‐
       sult.

